    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by high-efficiency upside and favorable environmental factors. The strongest play on the board is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.07), whose score is heavily buoyed by an Elite Dynamic Platoon advantage against Sproat and a wind-out scenario providing a lift to his base projection. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** (71.76) remains a set-and-forget start; despite a challenging L/L matchup against Rojas, his elite 0.425 xwOBA and the favorable 5.83 xERA of the opposing starter force him into the high-score tier. **Trea Turner** (71.38) and **Colt Keith** (68.01) round out our most potent offensive threats, with **Trea Turner** capitalizing on wind-aided potential and **Colt Keith** benefiting from a premium lineup spot and a favorable soft-tossing matchup against Cecconi.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the final UTIL slot, where **Hyeseong Kim** (47.43) narrowly edges out other options despite a suppressed score due to his #9 batting position and a 50% steal-prevention hold rate by King. We closely monitored **Caleb Durbin** as a potential substitute to prioritize the SB category, but he remains on the bench due to his current status outside the daily starting lineup, leaving **Hyeseong Kim** to navigate the marginal-tier workload. Managers should keep a close watch on **Christian Yelich** (54.28); while he starts today, his score reflects significant drag from the platoon disadvantage against Imanaga, placing him near the bottom of our recommended starters. We remain fully sidelined on **Zac Veen**, who continues his development in the minors, and **Kyle Schwarber**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, all of whom lack the active status or daily metrics to displace our current starters. We are monitoring for any late lineup changes that might impact **Dillon Dingler** or **Junior Caminero**, as both are currently operating with thin margins relative to their daily floor.",
